 262:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h **** /** \brief ACMD41, should be followed by CMD55, Response: R1\n
 263:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  * Sends host capacity support information (HCS) and asks the accessed card to send its operating c
 264:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  * in the response on the CMD line. HCS is effective when card receives SEND_IF_COND command.\n
 265:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  * Sends request to switch to 1.8V signaling (S18R). Reserved bit shall be set to '0'. CCS bit is a
 266:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  * XPC controls the maximum power in the default speed mode of SDXC card. XPC=0 means 0.36W (100mA 
 267:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  * but speed class is not supported. XPC=1 means 0.54W (150mA at 3.6V on VDD1) (max.) and speed cla
 268:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Sdmmc/Std/IfxSdmmc.h ****  */
